WEBVTT

00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:08.291
(Both gasp)

00:00:08.416 --> 00:00:12.250
Hurry up, lad!
We need those wheels out!

00:00:15.708 --> 00:00:18.000
(Madison) 'Embrace the risk, Henry.'

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:26.833
Embrace the risk...

00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:33.625
There you go.

00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:37.875
(All) Dad!

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:42.458
- Be with you in a minute!
- Oh, my goodness!

00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.083
- Let me take a photo!
- Forget the photo!

00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:46.583
No, do it! Do it!

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:48.958
My gosh!

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.208
(Groaning)

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:57.791
- You did it!
- Oh!

00:00:57.916 --> 00:01:00.208
- (Mrs Brown) Darling, well done!
- (Mr Brown) There you go.

00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:02.333
Home sweet home.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:06.833
That was amazing!

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:09.916
Well done, Mr Brown!
Nothing can go wrong now!

00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.083
(Screaming)

00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:18.166
Whoa... Oh!

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:21.458
Oh.

00:01:22.291 --> 00:01:23.708
Oh!

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.250
- Whoa!
- Bear!

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:30.416
Huh?

00:01:30.541 --> 00:01:32.875
(Screaming)

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.125
One of these must be
the windscreen wipers.

00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:40.041
(Screaming)

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:44.250
- Stop pushing buttons!
- I've got an idea!

00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:46.166
- (Mrs Brown) What?
- I'll need back-up.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.458
- Oh! Oh...
- (Bleating)

00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:52.875
Oh. Hello again.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.916
- Bear!
- Oh, dear.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:02.791
Erm... excuse me, Mr Llama,
could you please... giddy up?

00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:07.666
- Give me the bracelet, Bear!
- Oh... erm... Ah!

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:12.125
Ma-llama-lade.

00:02:12.916 --> 00:02:14.791
Hmm?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.833
(Jonathan) Hold me up!

00:02:19.291 --> 00:02:20.375
- Left a bit!
- Come on!

00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:23.916
- No! My left!
- Which left?

00:02:24.041 --> 00:02:25.375
- That left!
- That way?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.333
This left!

00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:28.375
Huh?

00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:33.625
Yes! Here we go.
Thank you. And this way!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.166
And I think it's up here.
Thank you.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.375
- Just round this corner...
- I need that bracelet!

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.083
I'm coming, Aunt Lucy!

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:48.416
Huh? Not you again?

00:02:48.541 --> 00:02:50.291
- Yes!
- (Screaming)

00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:54.333
Well done!

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.583
Gangway!

00:03:09.541 --> 00:03:11.041
(Sighs)

00:03:12.541 --> 00:03:15.041
- That was close.
- (Cracking)

00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:17.166
Oh...

00:03:17.291 --> 00:03:19.041
Extremely close.

00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:21.791
- Thank God!
- (Mr Brown) Well done, Jonathan!

00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:24.916
- Here we go! Brace positions!
- Okay.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:31.458
You really don't seem yourself,
Mr Hunter.

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.166
I am Gonzalo Caboto!

00:03:34.291 --> 00:03:36.666
- And I want my...
- (Engine approaching)

00:03:36.791 --> 00:03:40.458
♪ Onward Christian soldiers

00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:43.166
- ♪ Marching as to war
- (Jonathan) Why's she singing?

00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:47.750
- ♪ With the cross of Jesus... ♪
- (Screaming)

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:49.875
Oh, we've landed!

00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:56.541
(All) Whoa!

00:04:09.041 --> 00:04:10.875
(Groaning)

00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:14.375
(All) Ooh...

00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:30.458
(Gasps)

00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:32.500
Hmm?

00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:40.333
You looked like you enjoyed that!

00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:43.458
Oh! Oh, it's just so nice to...

00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:47.375
...all be on the same sofa again.

00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:51.625
(Mrs Bird) Well done,
Reverend Mother.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.750
Well done.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.291
(Mr Brown) Right, come on.
Out you go.

00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:00.166
We can all sing a hymn of thanks,
once we find Aunt Lucy.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.958
- Paddington!
- Mrs Brown!

00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:14.666
- Oh, Paddington!
- Paddington!

00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:18.625
(Mr Brown) Oh!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.125
- I'm so happy to see you all.
- Thank goodness you're all right.

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.916
- I knew this would come in handy.
- (Groaning)

00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:29.125
I know where Aunt Lucy is.

00:05:29.875 --> 00:05:32.541
She's somewhere behind this.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:36.000
And I think I know how to open it.

00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:39.916
Clever little bear.
I was rather hoping you would.

00:05:40.041 --> 00:05:41.250
Reverend Mother?

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.375
Oh!

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.291
- What on earth are you doing?
- Why, same as everyone else, my dear.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.125
Looking for gold.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:56.083
So, thank you very much for leading me
straight to it, as I knew you would.

00:05:56.208 --> 00:06:00.291
- This is a bit unchristian, isn't it?
- Well, it would be...

00:06:00.416 --> 00:06:02.750
...if I were really a nun.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.041
- Oh!
- Ooh! Oh, crikey.

00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:12.583
(Hunter) Clarissa?

00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:16.291
Cousin Clarissa?

00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:21.041
But you are dead.
You died in the jungle.

00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:24.291
- They're related?
- And you went to find yourself...?

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:27.208
No, I went to find gold!

00:06:27.958 --> 00:06:29.541
'And I never stopped looking.

00:06:29.666 --> 00:06:33.458
'And when I found out it had something
to do with bears, I did the obvious thing.

00:06:33.583 --> 00:06:37.583
'I disguised myself as a nun, and got a job
at the Home for Retired Bears.'

00:06:37.708 --> 00:06:40.208
Hello!
I'm your new Reverend Mother!

00:06:40.791 --> 00:06:42.708
Not that obvious.

00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:46.708
Years I was stuck there
with those mangy furbags.

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:48.083
How rude.

00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:52.208
Until one day,
Aunt Lucy showed me that bracelet.

00:06:52.333 --> 00:06:56.083
'And I knew that you would be the one
to lead me to El Dorado.'

00:06:57.375 --> 00:07:00.416
- Why me?
- Oh, she never told you?

00:07:00.541 --> 00:07:02.958
- It's your bracelet, Paddington.
- Oh?

00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:05.708
It was round your ankle
when she pulled you out of that river.

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:07.166
Hmm...

00:07:07.291 --> 00:07:10.875
I knew if anyone was gonna
show me the way, it would be you.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.666
So, I lured you to Peru, and I arranged
for your aunt's disappearance.

00:07:14.791 --> 00:07:17.000
(Gasps) Reverend Mother?

00:07:18.166 --> 00:07:23.083
Reverend Mother, I can't see you.
I-I can't see anything!

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:26.375
(Reverend Mother) 'I knew you'd
never rest until you found Aunt Lucy.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.375
'So, with a little help from me...

00:07:29.125 --> 00:07:30.708
'"Dear Paddington.

00:07:30.833 --> 00:07:36.375
'"I'm afraid I have some rather
worrying news about your Aunt Lucy.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.500
'"Please don't mention that I wrote.

00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:41.791
'"She wouldn't want you bothered
by such things."'

00:07:41.916 --> 00:07:43.791
You led me right here.

00:07:43.916 --> 00:07:47.458
So, please, give me that talisman.
Thank you.

00:07:47.583 --> 00:07:50.458
Oh, I don't seem to have it.

00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:55.291
- I really don't.
- Well, then, who has?

